### NOTE: SQL Server Agent should be up & running , then only we can get alerts.
  There are 3 types of Alerts;
               1.SQL server EVENT alerts
               2.SQL server PERFORMANCE alerts
               3.SQL server WMI

  1.SQL server EVENT alerts: 
            ## If we know the exact error number,then we can go with EVENT Alerts.
   (If any Login failures--> ERROR=18456
           Datafiles full---> ERROR=1105
           Logfiles full---> ERROR= 9002)

  go to SQL Server Agent----> (+) alerts (right click)----> new 
                                                  name= Login failure
                                                  type= event alert
                                                  error num= 18456
              ( check box) notify operator
                   select mail & ok.


2.SQL server PERFORMANCE alerts:
    ### If any performance issues like CPU, Memory, Blocking sessions, etc...
   go to alerts---> new alert--->name= cpu
                                 type= PERFORMANCE alerts
                                 obj= workload group stats
                                 counter= cpu usage%
                                 instance= internal
                                alert if counter: rises above
                                value=80
                   ( check box) Notify operators
                        select mail & ok.




              
